WEBVTT

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.000
For the sheep brain dissection, you will

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.000
need Carolina’s Perfect Solution sheep

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.000
brain with the dura mater removed,

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Carolina brain dissection mat, safety

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.000
glasses, laboratory apron, disposable

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.000
gloves, dissecting pan, and dissecting

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.000
kit. Place the sheep brain in the

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:28.000
dissecting tray, dorsal surface up.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.000
Observe and identify the following parts

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:34.000
of the brain: cerebrum, cerebellum,

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.000
spinal cord, medial longitudinal

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:41.000
fissure, right and left hemispheres,

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:45.000
olfactory bulb, and optic

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.000
nerve. Bisect the brain along the

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.000
medial longitudinal

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:00.000
fissure. Once bisected, observe the

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.000
internal anatomy of the brain and

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:07.000
identify the following structures: arbor

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.000
vitae, brain

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.000
stem, and

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:20.000
ventricles. Finally, cut across the

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:23.000
frontal lobe to identify white and gray

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:26.000
matter.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:28.000
The sheep brain dissection will help

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:30.000
students identify all major structures

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.000
of the brain, which can lead to further

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:37.000
discussions about the nervous system.
